  "scope": "Matched fresh control-before/control-after are the primary references for the two cold gap cycles. Older normal01..03 are separate historical context, never pooled into primary means/medians. First5ms excluded; all energy/means from finite native power/current windows.",
  "peak_definition": "Highest1ms or10ms current mean with window starts sampled every0.1ms from each queried interval start; this is a sampled search, not an exact sliding maximum. Different phase origins may produce slightly different maxima. Native instantaneous peak remains unqualified.",
  "gap_definition": "Direct markers11/12 after validated frame+sensorSTOP and beforeSDinit marker4. Gap baseline is last100ms before12, with electrically powered but uninitializedSD.",
  "limitations": [
    "Camera2->3 is directly comparable across all cold runs; camera2->11 is available only for gap runs and includes validation/STOP overhead.",
    "Actual capture, SD and whole-board demand may overlap; phase attribution is temporal, not per-component power.",
    "Excess over the quiet-gap floor subtracts whole-board mean power for an equal duration; it includes changing CPU/card/camera work and is not a measurement of a component rail or guaranteed removable energy.",
    "Artificial waiting adds energy and changes SD startup history; it is a diagnostic experiment, not automatically a better capture policy.",
    "Removing measured gap energy arithmetically does not predict a zero-gap implementation: ordering, timing and card startup history also changed.",
    "Card latency/slot occupancy varies; preserve per-run data and means/medians rather than assigning all timing changes to the gap.",
    "Native GPIO11/12 validates the gap boundary; RAM proof/readback remains separate evidence."
